<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
    SCHIENE HITCH-ADAPTER VISUAL (BUILD 18:52, FAILFIX of 18:26)

    Linked onto LoadPoint by DynamicallyLoadedParts with node="0". The loaded root is the
    SCENE, so ONE walk reaches this group; "0|0" walks twice and lands on the first Shape,
    which is why 1.2.5.80 shipped the frame alone with the pins and ball deleted.

    Geometry is inline IndexedTriangleSet in the shape the installed i3d-1.6.xsd defines:
    <v p n t0/> under Vertices, <t vi/> under Triangles, and the counts on Subset rather
    than on the IndexedTriangleSet element. No external .i3d.shapes: that binary is an
    undocumented Editor format and guessing it is not authoring.

    Orientation: tractor at -Z, Rainstar at +Z, from T32.i3d where attacherF sits at
    z -1.59 against wheels at z +1.58.

    schieneBall is the SPHERE ONLY. Its AABB centre is (0, -0.002, 0), which is
    AttacherJoint2 in LoadPoint space. The shank lives with the galvanized frame; when it
    shared the ball's shape the shape centre sat 15 mm off the joint and the drawbar eye
    would have floated beside the ball.

    Materials are vehicleShader, using the mod-local shader T32 and Aggregat already load
    and the stock neutral normal map. No invented texture, so no missing-map purple.

    Every Shape is renderable and collision-free. No dynamic, compound, density or
    collisionMask: a second rigid body changes the rest pose, which is the one-use-attach
    FAILFIX.
-->

